## 3. How projects connect to the 450 practice questions

We should not ask learners to repeat their earlier practice questions inside projects. Instead, projects should combine those concepts under new requirements.

| Project | Prerequisite practice categories                | New project-level challenge                  |
| ------- | ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| P01     | Filtering, strings, joins, aggregations         | Consistent retail reporting                  |
| P02     | Schemas, self joins, ranking                    | Workforce reporting with salary history      |
| P03     | GroupBy, conditional logic, windows             | Course completion and learner engagement     |
| P04     | Deduplication, anti joins, decimal types        | Ledger reconciliation and exception handling |
| P05     | Aggregations, time windows, feature preparation | Leakage-aware feature pipeline               |
| P06     | Parquet, joins, partitioning, explain plans     | Measurable query optimization                |
| P07     | Data quality, nested fields, Delta              | Validated multi-layer lakehouse              |
| P08     | MERGE, CDC, SCD2, idempotency                   | Correct historical state under replay        |
| P09     | JSON, event time, streaming joins               | Late-event-safe attribution                  |
| P10     | Stateful streaming, logging, recovery           | Resilient device monitoring                  |

This means all 90 lessons remain available as prerequisites, but learners do not need to finish every lesson before starting their first project. Each project should show its required skills and recommend relevant practice questions.

