Each milestone should include the task description, relevant tables, code editor, Run and Submit actions, test feedback, hints, and a clear output artifact. The learner can return later without losing code.

### Project grading

I recommend four separate checks:

| Dimension                                 | Weight |
| ----------------------------------------- | ------ |
| Correct outputs and business rules        | 50%    |
| Edge cases and data quality               | 20%    |
| Pipeline completeness and reproducibility | 20%    |
| Engineering-specific requirements         | 10%    |

For optimization projects, the last category should include benchmark evidence. For streaming projects, it should include replay and recovery behavior. A project must pass critical correctness and data-integrity gates regardless of its overall score.

Apache Spark's own testing utilities, including `assertDataFrameEqual` and `assertSchemaEqual`, give us a documented basis for the correctness checks.&#x20;

